---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Archived Redo"
  description="Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing archived redo generation, archive destinations, log history and archive gaps."
>
  <main>
    <section class="resource-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
        <h1>Archived <span class="hero-accent">Redo</span></h1>
        <p>
          Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing archived redo generation, archive
          destinations, log history and archive gaps.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resource-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="resource-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Understand how archived redo is being generated and stored</h2>
          <p>
            Archived redo provides the recovery history required for many
            backup, restore and Data Guard operations. Start with recent archive
            activity, then review destination status, redo sequences and any
            gaps that may affect recovery.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">01 &middot; RECENT ARCHIVE LOGS</div>
              <h2>Review recent archived redo</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Inspect the most recently archived redo logs, including thread, sequence, size and completion time.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    thread#,
    sequence#,
    first_time,
    next_time,
    completion_time,
    blocks,
    ROUND(blocks * block_size / 1024 / 1024, 2) AS size_mb,
    archived,
    applied
FROM v$archived_log
WHERE archived = 'YES'
ORDER BY completion_time DESC
FETCH FIRST 30 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">02 &middot; ARCHIVE DESTINATIONS</div>
              <h2>Review archive destination status</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Check the current status of configured archived redo destinations and the latest sequence sent to each one.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    dest_id,
    destination,
    status,
    target,
    archived_thread#,
    archived_seq#,
    error
FROM v$archive_dest_status
WHERE status NOT IN ('DEFERRED', 'INACTIVE')
ORDER BY dest_id;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">03 &middot; ARCHIVE HISTORY</div>
              <h2>Review redo generation by day</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Summarize archived redo volume by day to identify changes in workload and archive generation.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    TRUNC(completion_time) AS archive_day,
    COUNT(*) AS log_count,
    ROUND(
        SUM(blocks * block_size) / 1024 / 1024 / 1024,
        2
    ) AS size_gb
FROM v$archived_log
WHERE archived = 'YES'
GROUP BY TRUNC(completion_time)
ORDER BY archive_day DESC
FETCH FIRST 14 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">04 &middot; REDO THREADS</div>
              <h2>Review latest sequence by thread</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              In RAC environments, review the most recent archived sequence generated by each redo thread.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    thread#,
    MAX(sequence#) AS latest_sequence,
    MAX(completion_time) AS latest_archive_time
FROM v$archived_log
WHERE archived = 'YES'
GROUP BY thread#
ORDER BY thread#;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">05 &middot; ARCHIVE BACKUPS</div>
              <h2>Check archived redo backup coverage</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review archived redo records and identify logs that have not yet been backed up by RMAN.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    thread#,
    sequence#,
    completion_time,
    backup_count,
    name
FROM v$archived_log
WHERE archived = 'YES'
  AND backup_count = 0
ORDER BY completion_time DESC
FETCH FIRST 30 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">06 &middot; ARCHIVE GAPS</div>
              <h2>Check for an archive gap</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              On a physical standby, identify the current archived redo gap that is blocking recovery.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    thread#,
    low_sequence#,
    high_sequence#
FROM v$archive_gap
ORDER BY thread#;</code></pre>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-note">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Archived redo connects backup, recovery and Data Guard.</h2>
          <p>
            Review archive generation and destination status together rather
            than looking at a single archived log in isolation. Sequence
            history, backup coverage and archive gaps can provide important
            evidence when investigating recovery or standby synchronization
            problems.
          </p>
          <p>
            Oracle documents <code>V$ARCHIVED_LOG</code> as the source of
            archived log information from the control file,
            <code>V$ARCHIVE_DEST_STATUS</code> for runtime destination status,
            and <code>V$ARCHIVE_GAP</code> for the current archive gap on a
            standby database.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/tools/backup-recovery/">
            Back to Backup &amp; Recovery
          </a>
          <a
            class="resource-actions__link"
            href="/tools/backup-recovery/rman-recovery/"
          >
            Read RMAN Recovery
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".resource-block pre").forEach((pre) => {
    const button = document.createElement("button");
    button.type = "button";
    button.className = "resource-copy-button";
    button.textContent = "Copy";
    button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy SQL");

    pre.style.position = "relative";
    button.style.position = "absolute";
    button.style.top = "10px";
    button.style.right = "10px";
    button.style.padding = "5px 9px";
    button.style.border = "1px solid #d1d5db";
    button.style.borderRadius = "5px";
    button.style.background = "#ffffff";
    button.style.color = "#374151";
    button.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
    button.style.fontSize = "0.75rem";
    button.style.cursor = "pointer";
    button.style.zIndex = "2";

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const code = pre.querySelector("code");
      if (!code) return;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent || "");
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        button.textContent = "Copy failed";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      }
    });

    pre.appendChild(button);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .resource-hero {
    padding-top: 82px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .resource-hero h1 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 72px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .resource-hero .hero-accent {
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .resource-hero > .container > p:last-child {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-section {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }

  .resource-intro {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .resource-intro .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .resource-intro h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .resource-intro p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 22px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .resource-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    height: 560px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 30px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 18px;
    transition:
      border-color 0.22s ease,
      box-shadow 0.22s ease,
      transform 0.22s ease;
  }

  .resource-block:hover {
    border-color: #d8dce1;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(17, 29, 44, 0.06);
    transform: translateY(-3px);
  }

  .resource-block__header {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .resource-block__label {
    margin-bottom: 9px;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .resource-block h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .resource-block__description {
    min-height: 48px;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .resource-block pre {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-height: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 22px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-y: auto;
    white-space: pre;
    background: #2f353d;
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: #f3f4f6;
    font-family:
      "Cascadia Code",
      "Consolas",
      "Courier New",
      monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .resource-block code {
    font-family: inherit;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .resource-copy-button {
    position: absolute;
    top: 10px;
    right: 10px;
    padding: 5px 9px;
    border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #374151;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .resource-copy-button:hover {
    background: #f3f4f6;
  }

  .resource-note {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding: 30px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: #f7f8fa;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-note .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .resource-note h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .resource-note p:not(.eyebrow) {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .resource-note p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .resource-note code {
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #eef0f2;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family:
      "Cascadia Code",
      "Consolas",
      "Courier New",
      monospace;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }

  .resource-actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .resource-actions__link {
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .resource-actions__link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .resource-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .resource-hero {
      padding-top: 58px;
      padding-bottom: 54px;
    }

    .resource-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(38px, 12vw, 54px);
    }

    .resource-section {
      padding-top: 44px;
      padding-bottom: 56px;
    }

    .resource-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
    }

    .resource-block {
      height: 520px;
      padding: 22px;
      border-radius: 16px;
    }

    .resource-block__description {
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .resource-block pre {
      padding: 18px;
      font-size: 12px;
    }

    .resource-note {
      padding: 22px;
      border-radius: 16px;
    }

    .resource-actions {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
